<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Odo III, Duke of Burgundy</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1166–<a href="/years/1218">1218</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Odo III was duke of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/burgundy">Burgundy</a> from 1192 to 1218, the son of Hugh III. A loyal ally of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philip-ii-of-france">Philip II of France</a>, he fought at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-bouvines">Battle of Bouvines</a> in 1214 and took part in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/albigensian-crusade">Albigensian Crusade</a>. He died in 1218 while preparing to join the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fifth-crusade">Fifth Crusade</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/odo-iii-duke-of-burgundy.jpg" alt="Odo III, Duke of Burgundy" width="320" height="359" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Marquis de Migieu · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sceau_de_Eudes_III_Duc_de_Bourgogne.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
